@meta
id: 22-18
title: Drill — tick every box
chapter: 22
type: drill
skills: visual-block
par: 16
minutes: 4
reps: 8
vscode: click inside each pair of brackets, type x, eight times
open: checklist.md

@brief
Eight times: tick every box on the release checklist. The space inside
each `[ ]` becomes `x`.

`r` on a block replaces every character in the rectangle with the one
you press next. No insert mode, no `Esc`.

@keys
| `Ctrl-V` | start a block |
| `r` | replace every character in the block with the next key |

@hints
`2j` to the first item, `3l` to the space inside the brackets.
`Ctrl-V`, `7j`, `rx`.
--
`r` takes one character and finishes on its own. If you find yourself
pressing `Esc` afterwards, that is a habit, not a requirement.

@solution
    2 j 3 l Ctrl-V 7 j r x :wq<Enter>

Thirteen keystrokes. Block `r` is the fastest way to paint a column:
a column of spaces to `x`, a column of `,` to `;`, a column of `-` to
`|`. The reverse of this drill — untick every box — is the same keys
with `r` followed by a space.

@start checklist.md
# Release checklist

- [ ] Migrations applied to staging
- [ ] Refund window verified against finance sheet
- [ ] Order cutoff hour confirmed with ops
- [ ] Payment retries observed in logs
- [ ] Customer email template signed off
- [ ] Reconcile export sent to finance
- [ ] Registry split deployed
- [ ] Changelog updated

@expected checklist.md
# Release checklist

- [x] Migrations applied to staging
- [x] Refund window verified against finance sheet
- [x] Order cutoff hour confirmed with ops
- [x] Payment retries observed in logs
- [x] Customer email template signed off
